===Etymology===
Probably related to {{m|de|Zinke||point, prong}}, from {{der|de|goh|zint||a jag, point}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*tinduz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*tindaz||prong, pinnacle}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*(e)dont-||tooth, projection}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|tinne||battlement}}, {{cog|de|Zinne||pinnacle, battlement}}, {{cog|da|tinde||pinnacle, battlement}}, {{cog|sv|tinne||tooth of a rake}}, {{cog|is|tindur||spike, tooth of a rake or harrow, pinnacle, peak, battlement}}.

